1
00:00:03,524 --> 00:00:04,942
اَعُوْذُ بِاللهِ مِنَّ الشِّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيْمِ۝

2
00:00:04,967 --> 00:00:06,267
بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيْمَ۝

3
00:00:06,291 --> 00:00:12,273
اَلْحَمْدُ لله  وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرا

4
00:00:13,332 --> 00:00:18,562
We talked about the Makkan era, we completed it.

5
00:00:19,105 --> 00:00:21,463
We talked about the Islam of Abu Bakr Siddique رضي الله عنه

6
00:00:21,599 --> 00:00:28,314
background before Islam, his family, Da'wah(دعوة), the trials he went through in Makkah.

7
00:00:28,810 --> 00:00:31,225
In the first session, we talked about Al-Isra Wal Miraj(اسراء ولمعراج)

8
00:00:31,815 --> 00:00:33,472
and we talked about Al-Hijrah(هجرة).

9
00:00:33,850 --> 00:00:37,992
So we're done with the Makkah era which was 13 years.

10
00:00:38,246 --> 00:00:41,667
Now we'll move on to the Madina era

11
00:00:42,174 --> 00:00:50,143
and we'll devote this session to the participation of Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه in Jihad(جهاد) with Rasool Allah ﷺ.

12
00:00:50,677 --> 00:00:53,178
That's what we're going to talk about In Sha Allah Ho Ta'ala(ان شاء الله تعالى), this evening.

13
00:00:55,729 --> 00:00:59,336
To sum it up, Ibn Kathir(ابن كثير) says in Al-Bidaya Wan Nihaya(البدايه والنهايه).

14
00:01:00,020 --> 00:01:05,458
ولم يختلف أهل السير في أنَّ  أبا بكر ألصديق رضي الله عنه

15
00:01:05,815 --> 00:01:12,451
لم يتخلف عن الرسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم  في مشهدٍ من مشاهده كُلِّهَا

16
00:01:13,724 --> 00:01:18,794
Ibn Kathir(ابن كثير) says: It is the consensus among the scholars of history

17
00:01:19,493 --> 00:01:26,164
that Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه has never missed any of the conquests of Rasool Allah ﷺ

18
00:01:27,160 --> 00:01:30,232
he was there, all the time in every single one, of them.

19
00:01:31,553 --> 00:01:36,894
With many of the other Sahabah(صحابه) they ended up missing some because of various reasons,

20
00:01:37,417 --> 00:01:43,946
but Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه was always on the side of Rasool Allah ﷺ

21
00:01:44,044 --> 00:01:45,198
he never missed anything.

22
00:01:46,420 --> 00:01:49,171
There's another statement from Zamakhshari(زمخشري), he says:

23
00:01:49,767 --> 00:01:58,361
إنَّه’ كانَ مضافًا برسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم إلى الأبد فَإنه’ صاحبه’ صغيرًا وأنفقَ ماله’ كبيرا

24
00:01:58,733 --> 00:02:01,917
وحمله’ إلى المدينة براحلته وذاد

25
00:02:02,254 --> 00:02:07,081
ولم يزل ينفق عليه ماله’ في حياته وزوجه’ابْنَتًا

26
00:02:07,407 --> 00:02:10,589
 ولم يزل ملازمًا له سفرًا وحضرَا

27
00:02:10,824 --> 00:02:16,618
فلمَّا توفيَّ دفنه’ في حجرة عائشه أحبُّ النِّساء إليه صلى الله عليه وسلم

28
00:02:17,528 --> 00:02:27,671
That Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه, his name will always go side by side with the name of Muhammadﷺ,

29
00:02:28,065 --> 00:02:30,840
 because he was his friend when he was young.

30
00:02:31,193 --> 00:02:34,214
And he was his financial supporter, when he was old.

31
00:02:34,758 --> 00:02:38,471
He carried him to Madina on his own camel

32
00:02:39,150 --> 00:02:41,575
and he provided for him in that journey.

33
00:02:42,243 --> 00:02:45,808
And he continued supporting Rasool Allah ﷺ

34
00:02:46,577 --> 00:02:50,069
and he married Rasool Allah ﷺ, his daughter,

35
00:02:50,529 --> 00:02:57,042
and he was always accompanying him, whether he was a resident, or a traveler.

36
00:02:57,509 --> 00:03:04,694
And when Rasool Allah ﷺ passed away he buried him, in the room of his daughter, Ayesha رضي الله عنها

37
00:03:04,935 --> 00:03:08,167
who was the most beloved person to Muhammadﷺ.

38
00:03:10,898 --> 00:03:18,136
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه would also lead armies that were sent by Rasool Allah ﷺ.

39
00:03:18,182 --> 00:03:20,857
For example Salama Ibn Akwa(سلمه إبن أكوع), he says:

40
00:03:21,134 --> 00:03:25,578
غزوة مع نبي صلى الله عليه وسلم سبعة غزواتٍ

41
00:03:26,031 --> 00:03:34,200
وخرجت فيما يبعث من البعوث تسعه غزواتٍ مرة علينا أبوبكر ومرَّة علينا أسامه

42
00:03:34,775 --> 00:03:42,448
Salama Ibn Akwa(سلمه إبن أكوع) said: I have participated in seven of the battles of Rasool Allah ﷺ

43
00:03:42,980 --> 00:03:49,566
 and I have went out in some of the armies that Muhammadﷺ would send out, nine times

44
00:03:49,586 --> 00:03:53,263
 actually he says that I have joined in seven armies with Rasool Allah ﷺ

45
00:03:53,626 --> 00:03:57,747
and I have joined in nine armies that he sent out.

46
00:03:58,009 --> 00:04:00,884
Sometimes he would appoint Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) to be our leader

47
00:04:01,060 --> 00:04:04,821
and sometimes he would appoint Osama bin Zayed(أسامه بن زيد), to be our leader.

48
00:04:05,271 --> 00:04:10,642
So Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه would also lead, armies.

49
00:04:12,376 --> 00:04:16,447
We'll talk about some events that happened with him, in these conquests.

50
00:04:16,582 --> 00:04:22,305
In the Battle of Badr(بدر), when Rasool Allah ﷺ was seeking the advice of the Sahabah(صحابه)

51
00:04:22,629 --> 00:04:26,100
on whether to go ahead and confront the army of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

52
00:04:26,124 --> 00:04:29,652
Because remember that they went out for a completely different purpose.

53
00:04:29,676 --> 00:04:35,364
They went to take over a caravan of the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ),

54
00:04:35,899 --> 00:04:38,521
but then they ended up meeting the army.

55
00:04:39,385 --> 00:04:43,443
So Rasool Allah ﷺ was seeking the advice of the Sahabah(صحابه), on what to do.?

56
00:04:44,518 --> 00:04:49,045
The first one to stand up and speak was, Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه.

57
00:04:51,557 --> 00:04:56,456
Usually, in every situation, when Rasool Allah ﷺ is seeking counsel

58
00:04:57,234 --> 00:04:59,948
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه would be the first to speak.

59
00:05:01,077 --> 00:05:03,581
Sometimes there would be other speakers, after him.

60
00:05:03,789 --> 00:05:05,882
Sometimes he would be the only one to speak.

61
00:05:06,418 --> 00:05:09,452
And Rasool Allah ﷺ would end up following his opinion.

62
00:05:10,082 --> 00:05:14,924
So, the most prominent role that both Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and Umar(عُمَر) played

63
00:05:15,265 --> 00:05:19,195
were the advisors of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

64
00:05:21,613 --> 00:05:25,485
When Rasool Allah ﷺ was with his army and

65
00:05:26,397 --> 00:05:29,755
so you have Rasool Allah ﷺ with his army in Badr(بدر).

66
00:05:29,995 --> 00:05:32,534
And then you have Mushrikeen(مشركين) coming out from Makkah

67
00:05:33,131 --> 00:05:37,113
and both armies do not know, where the enemy is.

68
00:05:38,070 --> 00:05:40,717
Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) are unaware of the position of Muhammadﷺ,

69
00:05:40,741 --> 00:05:44,598
and Muhammadﷺ is unaware of the position of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

70
00:05:44,747 --> 00:05:50,640
It wasn't that they had a set appointment everyone was trying to catch the other.

71
00:05:51,237 --> 00:05:55,022
So Rasool Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) they went out around the army

72
00:05:55,716 --> 00:05:58,213
and they walked away in the distance.

73
00:05:59,386 --> 00:06:01,660
So they ended up meeting an old Bedouin.

74
00:06:03,665 --> 00:06:07,299
Rasool Allah ﷺ walked up to this Bedouin and he asked him, he said:

75
00:06:08,335 --> 00:06:12,534
Have you heard anything about the army of Muhammad(محمد) and the army of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

76
00:06:13,451 --> 00:06:15,501
This man doesn't know who he is speaking to.

77
00:06:17,379 --> 00:06:18,436
So the old man said:

78
00:06:18,502 --> 00:06:21,825
If you tell me who you are! I'm going to tell you where they are!

79
00:06:22,837 --> 00:06:26,233
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: If you tell us, we will tell you!

80
00:06:28,386 --> 00:06:37,704
He said: Someone told me that Muhammadﷺ and his army have left Madina on such and such date.

81
00:06:38,245 --> 00:06:43,084
If the information is correct then now they would be in such and such place.

82
00:06:43,515 --> 00:06:46,767
And he pointed out the right position of the Muslim army.

83
00:06:47,256 --> 00:06:49,026
So that was an indication of his truth.

84
00:06:51,830 --> 00:06:58,529
And I've received information that the army of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) have leaved on such and such date,

85
00:06:58,791 --> 00:07:02,400
 and if that information is correct then they would be in such and such place.

86
00:07:03,839 --> 00:07:06,492
So now he gave his information.

87
00:07:06,985 --> 00:07:09,839
He asked Rasool Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr(ابوبكر): Who are you?

88
00:07:10,348 --> 00:07:13,445
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: "We are from water", and he walked away.

89
00:07:14,597 --> 00:07:18,678
So the old man was flipping his hands and saying: What from water.?

90
00:07:18,719 --> 00:07:21,407
Are you from the water of the Iraq, the rivers of the Iraq?

91
00:07:21,919 --> 00:07:25,917
What Rasool Allah ﷺ meant is that were created from water, Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says,

92
00:07:26,569 --> 00:07:27,906
وَجَعَلْنَا مِنَ الْمَاء كُلَّ شَيْءٍ حَيٍّ

93
00:07:27,930 --> 00:07:30,762
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ has made every living being out of water.

94
00:07:32,028 --> 00:07:34,794
And Rasool Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه left.

95
00:07:35,431 --> 00:07:41,301
You have to have that wisdom in situations of war, and in Islam you cannot lie.

96
00:07:41,688 --> 00:07:44,371
So Rasool Allah ﷺ spoke the truth,

97
00:07:44,791 --> 00:07:49,224
but it was packaged in a way that the listener would understand something,

98
00:07:49,561 --> 00:07:52,089
while Rasool Allah ﷺ means something else.

99
00:07:52,445 --> 00:07:56,257
And you can see the wisdom of Rasool Allah ﷺ in such a response

100
00:07:56,519 --> 00:07:59,914
and he was able to extract the information from the man, peacefully.

101
00:08:01,948 --> 00:08:05,651
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه was with him, that's the point of mentioning this story

102
00:08:05,675 --> 00:08:09,805
that the Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه was always accompanying Muhammad صلوات الله وسلام عليه.

103
00:08:10,216 --> 00:08:13,480
And when it was right before the Battle of Badr(بدر)

104
00:08:14,652 --> 00:08:17,837
Rasool Allah ﷺ wanted to be with the army, fighting in the frontline

105
00:08:17,861 --> 00:08:22,251
but the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم told Muhammad صلوات الله وسلام عليه: No,

106
00:08:22,701 --> 00:08:26,193
We want you to be in the back of the army.

107
00:08:26,717 --> 00:08:29,725
We'll build a shed for you and you will stay there.

108
00:08:30,408 --> 00:08:38,018
So that if we lose, then you can take the other Sahabah(صحابه), who remained

109
00:08:38,554 --> 00:08:42,375
and go back to Madina and continue the fight from there.

110
00:08:43,463 --> 00:08:45,852
Rasool Allah ﷺ liked the idea

111
00:08:46,130 --> 00:08:50,352
so they prepared a shed for him behind the lines

112
00:08:51,317 --> 00:08:54,364
and Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه was one guarding him.

113
00:08:54,389 --> 00:08:56,825
And I mentioned that, and I'll not repeat the story again,

114
00:08:56,969 --> 00:09:00,659
when Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) stood on the Mimbar(ممبر) and said, "Who's the most courageous"?

115
00:09:01,042 --> 00:09:06,380
And he mentioned the story of seeing Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه carrying his sword

116
00:09:06,743 --> 00:09:10,552
surrounding the tent, protecting Rasool Allah ﷺ from every direction.

117
00:09:12,345 --> 00:09:22,440
Rasool Allah ﷺ was making Dua(دُعَا) before the battle, standing up, raising his hands and making Dua(دُعَا) to Allah.

118
00:09:24,408 --> 00:09:27,935
A very long Dua(دُعَا), he was very involved in the Dua(دُعَا).

119
00:09:29,337 --> 00:09:32,608
He had a cloth covering his shoulders

120
00:09:33,036 --> 00:09:37,346
and he was raising his hands and making Dua(دُعَا) and he was so involved in the Dua(دُعَا),

121
00:09:38,241 --> 00:09:40,534
the cloth on his shoulders fell down.

122
00:09:42,511 --> 00:09:43,283
And he was saying:

123
00:09:43,307 --> 00:09:45,478
أللهم إنجزلي موعدتني

124
00:09:45,865 --> 00:09:48,651
O Allah, fulfill Your promise to me.

125
00:09:49,297 --> 00:09:53,908
فَإنك أن تُھلكَ هذه العصاب من أهل الإسلام فلا تُعبد في الأرض أبدًا

126
00:09:54,108 --> 00:10:02,305
Because if you decree that this band of Muslims perish then you're not gonna be worshiped on Earth.

127
00:10:04,907 --> 00:10:08,115
The only Muslims on the face of the earth are the ones here.

128
00:10:09,581 --> 00:10:14,401
This is Islam, if they die, then no one will worship you Oh Allah.

129
00:10:14,963 --> 00:10:19,494
Ya'ani(يعني) you can see, how dark the world was and this was the only beacon of light

130
00:10:19,770 --> 00:10:21,526
the Muslims who were in the Battle of Badr(بدر).

131
00:10:23,975 --> 00:10:25,246
And he is saying: O Allah

132
00:10:25,271 --> 00:10:26,215
إنجزلي موعدتني

133
00:10:26,286 --> 00:10:28,073
So, O Allah fulfill Your promise to me!

134
00:10:28,381 --> 00:10:35,550
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه, he picked up the cloth of Rasool Allah ﷺ and he put it back on his shoulders.

135
00:10:36,518 --> 00:10:38,365
 And then he said, "O Messenger of Allah!

136
00:10:38,389 --> 00:10:43,718
كفاك مناشدتَك ربك فإنَّ الله مُنْجُزٌلَكَ موعدك

137
00:10:44,402 --> 00:10:47,099
O Messenger of Allah! that is enough.

138
00:10:48,081 --> 00:10:51,933
Because Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ will fulfill His promise to you, that's enough!

139
00:10:52,492 --> 00:10:54,721
Allah will fulfill His promise to you.

140
00:10:55,920 --> 00:11:00,091
So Rasool Allah ﷺ went back to the tent, and he fell asleep.

141
00:11:02,963 --> 00:11:04,898
He slept right before the battle.

142
00:11:06,224 --> 00:11:11,393
 And this happened with the Muslims a few times in the battle, they would have An-Na'as(ألنعاس),

143
00:11:11,848 --> 00:11:15,254
they would fall asleep for a moment, and it happened to them in Badr(بدر).

144
00:11:15,278 --> 00:11:17,941
إِذْ يُغَشِّيكُمُ النُّعَاسَ أَمَنَةً مِنْهُ

145
00:11:18,187 --> 00:11:21,999
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says: And you slept and it was tranquility from Allah.

146
00:11:22,238 --> 00:11:29,488
So the scholars say: If someone sleeps in the battlefield, that is from Allah

147
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:33,681
and if somebody sleeps or feels sleepy in Salah(صلاة), that is from Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ).

148
00:11:35,372 --> 00:11:43,492
If you feel the urge to sleep, in the battlefield, An-Na'as(ألنعاس), slumber, that is from Allah.

149
00:11:44,191 --> 00:11:46,932
 If you feel it in Salah(صلاة), that is from Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ).

150
00:11:47,790 --> 00:11:52,423
So Rasool Allah ﷺ fell asleep and then he suddenly woke up and he said:

151
00:11:52,447 --> 00:11:54,467
أبشر أبابكربنصرالله

152
00:11:54,799 --> 00:11:58,152
O Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) rejoice with the victory of Allah

153
00:11:58,383 --> 00:12:01,388
Here comes Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل) riding his horse.

154
00:12:02,185 --> 00:12:04,560
And that's when Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ revealed Ayaat(آيات):

155
00:12:04,878 --> 00:12:11,742
إِذْ تَسْتَغِيثُونَ رَبَّكُمْ فَاسْتَجابَ لَكُمْ أَنِّي مُمِدُّكُمْ بِأَلْفٍ مِنَ الْمَلائِكَةِ مُرْدِفِينَ

156
00:12:12,356 --> 00:12:19,751
وَما جَعَلَهُ اللَّهُ إِلاَّ بُشْرى وَلِتَطْمَئِنَّ بِهِ قُلُوبُكُمْ وَمَا النَّصْرُ إِلاَّ مِنْ عِنْدِ اللَّهِ إِنَّ اللَّهَ عَزِيزٌ حَكِيمٌ۝

157
00:12:20,130 --> 00:12:22,354
In one Qira'ah(قراءة) Murdafeen(مُرْدَفِينَ), in another Qira'ah(قراءة) Murdifeen(مُرْدِفِينَ).

158
00:12:23,772 --> 00:12:27,797
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says: Remember when you asked help of Your Lord

159
00:12:28,528 --> 00:12:35,750
and He answered you, Indeed, I will reinforce you with 1000 from the angels following one another.

160
00:12:36,493 --> 00:12:38,961
 And Allah made it not but good tiding

161
00:12:39,387 --> 00:12:44,959
and so that your hearts would be assured, thereby and victory is not but from Allah.

162
00:12:45,186 --> 00:12:47,052
Indeed, Allah is Exalted in Mighty and Wise.

163
00:12:47,076 --> 00:12:51,844
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ is saying: You asked for help, Rasool Allah ﷺ was making that long Dua(دُعَا)

164
00:12:52,400 --> 00:12:58,380
you asked for help, so I gave it to you, 1000 Angels and in one narration 2000 Angels

165
00:12:58,774 --> 00:13:03,348
one following the other, and they are led by Jibreel عليه السّلام and Mikaeel عليه السّلام.

166
00:13:04,008 --> 00:13:07,616
But Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says: "The only reason I sent you these angels

167
00:13:08,050 --> 00:13:12,149
is to give you comfort in your hearts, because victory is from Me.

168
00:13:12,170 --> 00:13:16,036
You don't need the angels for that, I will give you victory, you're gonna get it

169
00:13:16,237 --> 00:13:20,944
but just so that I will please the heart of Rasool Allah ﷺ and the hearts of the Muslims.

170
00:13:21,230 --> 00:13:24,231
I'm sending you down these angels to support you,

171
00:13:25,454 --> 00:13:26,789
وَمَا النَّصْرُ إِلاَّ مِنْ عِنْدِ اللَّهِ

172
00:13:26,814 --> 00:13:29,720
Because victory only comes from Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

173
00:13:30,346 --> 00:13:35,025
In the fighting Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه joined in, as he would in every battle.

174
00:13:35,826 --> 00:13:39,360
Years later, when his son Abdur Rahman(عبدالرحمن) became Muslim

175
00:13:39,528 --> 00:13:42,937
and he only became Muslim in the six year of Hijrah(هجرة).

176
00:13:43,496 --> 00:13:47,038
So Abdur Rahman(عبدالرحمن) was the last member of the family of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) to become Muslim.

177
00:13:47,712 --> 00:13:49,990
So he fought against the Muslims in the Battle of Badr(بدر).

178
00:13:50,127 --> 00:13:54,276
Abdur Rahman(عبدالرحمن) later on, told his father when he was a Muslim, he said;

179
00:13:54,968 --> 00:13:59,669
"On the day of Badr(بدر), you were in my sights", he was an archer.

180
00:14:00,525 --> 00:14:05,677
"You're in my sights, but I turned away from you, because I didn't want to kill you."

181
00:14:07,400 --> 00:14:09,575
Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) responded by saying,

182
00:14:09,922 --> 00:14:14,291
"On the day of Badr(بدر) I never saw you, but if I did, I would have killed you."

183
00:14:16,764 --> 00:14:20,848
Look at the Eeman(ايمان) of Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه

184
00:14:20,879 --> 00:14:25,310
because that's what he understood from the Qur'an, Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says:

185
00:14:25,334 --> 00:14:34,861
قُلْ إِن كَانَ آبَاؤُكُمْ وَأَبْنَاؤُكُمْ وَإِخْوَانُكُمْ وَأَزْوَاجُكُمْ وَعَشِيرَتُكُمْ وَأَمْوَالٌ اقْتَرَفْتُمُوهَا وَتِجَارَةٌ تَخْشَوْنَ كَسَادَهَا

186
00:14:35,654 --> 00:14:43,565
وَمَسَاكِنُ تَرْضَوْنَهَا أَحَبَّ إِلَيْكُم مِّنَ اللَّهِ وَرَسُولِهِ وَجِهَادٍ فِي سَبِيلِهِ فَتَرَبَّصُوا حَتَّىٰ يَأْتِيَ اللَّهُ بِأَمْرِهِ ۗ

187
00:14:44,077 --> 00:14:49,568
Say O Muhammad(محمد), if your fathers, your sons, your brothers,

188
00:14:49,744 --> 00:14:53,823
your wives, your relatives, wealth which you have obtained

189
00:14:54,182 --> 00:14:58,660
commerce wherein you fear decline and dwellings with which you are pleased

190
00:14:59,031 --> 00:15:04,459
are more beloved to you, then Allah and His messenger, and Jihad(جهاد) in His cause

191
00:15:04,652 --> 00:15:09,429
then wait until Allah executes His command, and Allah does not guide

192
00:15:09,738 --> 00:15:11,605
the defiantly disobedient people".

193
00:15:12,519 --> 00:15:16,556
You need to put Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ and Muhammadﷺ and the Jihad(جهاد) in the sake of Allah

194
00:15:16,779 --> 00:15:18,976
before your father's your sons, your wives

195
00:15:19,000 --> 00:15:21,838
your families, your business, your dwellings before everything.

196
00:15:24,371 --> 00:15:27,731
The battle was over! Decisive Victory for the Muslims!

197
00:15:28,071 --> 00:15:30,536
This was the first battle between Eeman(ايمان) and Kuffr(كفر).

198
00:15:31,087 --> 00:15:35,674
When Rasool Allah ﷺ was in his tent watching the battlefield

199
00:15:37,678 --> 00:15:42,976
and the Kuffar(كفار) of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) lost with him was Saad Bin Muadh رضي الله عنه.

200
00:15:44,480 --> 00:15:46,573
Saad Bin Muadh(سعد بن معاذ) was watching what was happening

201
00:15:46,597 --> 00:15:52,419
the Muslims are now tying the Kuffar(كفار) in ropes, Prisoners Of War.

202
00:15:52,980 --> 00:15:56,475
 Saad Bin Muadh(سعد بن معاذ) his face didn't look pleased.

203
00:15:56,557 --> 00:16:01,963
So Rasool Allah ﷺ said: O Saad(سعد) it seems that you are not happy with what is happening".

204
00:16:03,107 --> 00:16:08,252
Saad(سعد) said: "Yes, I'm not, because this was the first day in which we meet Kuffr(كفر).

205
00:16:08,920 --> 00:16:12,114
So we should have executed them rather than taking them prisoners of war.

206
00:16:13,829 --> 00:16:15,780
70 of them were taken prisoners of war

207
00:16:15,804 --> 00:16:19,364
and Rasool Allah ﷺ wanted to know what to do with them.

208
00:16:19,502 --> 00:16:21,249
This was the first time it happens.

209
00:16:22,162 --> 00:16:25,929
So he was seeking counsel advise from the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم.

210
00:16:26,984 --> 00:16:28,136
What shall we do with them?

211
00:16:29,650 --> 00:16:32,632
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه again the first man to stand up, he said:

212
00:16:32,707 --> 00:16:38,406
O Messenger of Allah, these are our brothers, our fathers, and our relatives

213
00:16:40,578 --> 00:16:47,115
I think that we should ransom them, because the money would strengthen us against disbelief

214
00:16:47,924 --> 00:16:52,269
 and maybe one day, these people would become Muslim.

215
00:16:54,257 --> 00:17:00,715
Now that the battle is over, Abu Bakr رضي الله عنه is showing the merciful side.

216
00:17:01,305 --> 00:17:04,543
In the battle he said: If he saw his son he would kill him but now the battle is over.

217
00:17:05,307 --> 00:17:08,435
Let's free them.! The money will benefit us.

218
00:17:08,923 --> 00:17:11,427
and maybe one day they will become Muslim.

219
00:17:13,095 --> 00:17:16,241
The next in line was Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب), he stood up and said:

220
00:17:16,265 --> 00:17:20,052
"O Messenger of Allah, I do not agree with what Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) said,

221
00:17:21,275 --> 00:17:26,829
I think you should hand over the relative of Ali(علي) to Ali(علي) for him to execute

222
00:17:26,860 --> 00:17:30,159
you hand me over my relative so that I would execute him

223
00:17:30,359 --> 00:17:34,651
and you hand over every Muslim their relatives from among the disbelievers.

224
00:17:34,676 --> 00:17:36,453
So that they execute them,

225
00:17:36,874 --> 00:17:42,247
until the disbelievers understand that we have no leniency in our hearts towards them.

226
00:17:43,530 --> 00:17:46,471
So he wanted the execution of all of these prisoners of war.

227
00:17:47,889 --> 00:17:53,681
Two different view points, opposite of each other, differences of opinion.

228
00:17:54,622 --> 00:17:56,488
How did Rasool Allah ﷺ deal with that?

229
00:17:57,754 --> 00:18:04,421
Because we have differences of opinion between us, some are towards the firm side

230
00:18:04,667 --> 00:18:06,620
and some are towards the lenient side.

231
00:18:07,827 --> 00:18:14,109
That's the nature of man, but the case now is that everybody is disapproving the other strongly

232
00:18:15,569 --> 00:18:22,077
 that there is no room for dialogue, no room for unity and its very unfortunate.

233
00:18:23,255 --> 00:18:27,067
Differences did exist among the Sahabah(صحابه) because every person is different.

234
00:18:27,908 --> 00:18:31,726
And your views, the way you see the world

235
00:18:32,178 --> 00:18:36,962
the lenses that you have on your eyes are based on your knowledge

236
00:18:37,326 --> 00:18:43,100
your experience, your background, all of those influence the way you view the world.

237
00:18:43,924 --> 00:18:48,344
The experience of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was different then the experience of Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه

238
00:18:48,536 --> 00:18:50,744
that's why they would see things in a different color.?

239
00:18:52,021 --> 00:18:53,854
Now look at the response of Rasool Allah ﷺ

240
00:18:53,959 --> 00:19:01,532
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ makes the hearts of some men, softer than milk

241
00:19:03,670 --> 00:19:09,479
and Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ makes the hearts of some men against the enemies of Allah, firmer than stone.

242
00:19:11,565 --> 00:19:16,270
And the analogy of you, O Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) is like Ibrahim عليه السّلام who said:

243
00:19:18,120 --> 00:19:23,043
فَمَن تَبِعَنِى فَإِنَّهُۥ مِنِّى ۖ وَمَنْ عَصَانِى فَإِنَّكَ غَفُورٌ رَّحِيمٌ۝

244
00:19:24,445 --> 00:19:27,100
Whoever follows me, belongs to me.

245
00:19:27,266 --> 00:19:29,765
And whoever doesn't Allah is Forgiving and Merciful.

246
00:19:31,574 --> 00:19:36,408
And the analogy of you Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) is also like Eesa عليه السّلام, who said;

247
00:19:36,600 --> 00:19:43,014
إِنْ تُعَذِّبْهُمْ فَإِنَّهُمْ عِبَادُكَ وَإِنْ تَغْفِرْ لَهُمْ فَإِنَّكَ أَنْتَ الْعَزِيزُ الْحَكِيمُ۝

248
00:19:43,425 --> 00:19:47,578
If You should punish them, indeed they are Your servants

249
00:19:47,910 --> 00:19:53,478
but if you forgive them, indeed it is You, Who is Exalted in Might, the Wise.

250
00:19:54,029 --> 00:20:02,371
Ibrahim عليه السّلام and Eesa عليه السّلام showed the forbearance side the compassionate side towards their enemies,

251
00:20:03,252 --> 00:20:04,663
and then Rasool Allah ﷺ said:

252
00:20:04,750 --> 00:20:10,563
And the analogy of you, O Umar(عُمَر) is like Nooh عليه السّلام, who said;

253
00:20:11,153 --> 00:20:15,085
وَقَالَ نُوحٌ رَّبِّ لَا تَذَرْ عَلَى الْأَرْضِ مِنَ الْكَافِرِينَ دَيَّارًا

254
00:20:15,626 --> 00:20:21,018
And Nooh(نوح) said, "My Lord, Do not leave upon the earth from among the believers an inhabitant,

255
00:20:21,249 --> 00:20:24,109
Wipe them out, Don't leave any disbeliever,

256
00:20:25,292 --> 00:20:30,250
And the analogy of you Umar(عُمَر) is also like, Musa عليه السّلام, who said;

257
00:20:30,801 --> 00:20:40,137
وَقَالَ مُوسَىٰ رَبَّنَا إِنَّكَ ءَاتَيْتَ فِرْعَوْنَ وَمَلَأَهُۥ زِينَةً وَأَمْوَٰلًا فِى ٱلْحَيَوٰةِ ٱلدُّنْيَا رَبَّنَا لِيُضِلُّواْ عَن سَبِيلِكَ

258
00:20:40,414 --> 00:20:46,339
رَبَّنَا ٱطْمِسْ عَلَىٰ أَمْوَٰلِهِمْ وَٱشْدُدْ عَلَىٰ قُلُوبِهِمْ فَلَا يُؤْمِنُواْ حَتَّىٰ يَرَوُاْ ٱلْعَذَابَ ٱلْأَلِيمَ۝

259
00:20:47,582 --> 00:20:51,700
And Musa(موسى) said: Our Lord, Indeed you have given Pharaoh

260
00:20:51,725 --> 00:20:56,096
and his establishment splendor and wealth in the worldly life.

261
00:20:56,483 --> 00:21:00,601
Our Lord, that they may lead men astray from Your way.

262
00:21:00,902 --> 00:21:06,075
Our Lord obliterate their wealth and harden their hearts so that they will not believe

263
00:21:06,100 --> 00:21:08,424
until they see the painful punishment.

264
00:21:09,264 --> 00:21:14,222
Musa(موسى) is saying that "Firaun(فرعون) and his establishment are using their wealth

265
00:21:14,836 --> 00:21:17,018
to mislead people from the true path.

266
00:21:17,318 --> 00:21:22,874
Therefore O Allah, destroy their wealth and harden their hearts so that they don't believe.

267
00:21:22,999 --> 00:21:25,904
Because these people deserve the punishment, they don't deserve Jannah(جنة)

268
00:21:27,651 --> 00:21:30,493
and these are Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) of Allah and they would view things differently,

269
00:21:31,357 --> 00:21:32,853
personalities are different.

270
00:21:34,534 --> 00:21:39,797
Ibrahim عليه السّلام when he received the news of the destruction of the people of Lut(لوط).

271
00:21:39,984 --> 00:21:40,860
What did he do?

272
00:21:41,142 --> 00:21:44,811
The first thing he remembered was to argue on behalf of Lut(لوط)

273
00:21:45,383 --> 00:21:47,965
because Lut(لوط) was still there and Ibrahim عليه السّلام was worried

274
00:21:48,180 --> 00:21:50,819
that if the punishment of Allah comes on the people of Lut(لوط).

275
00:21:51,120 --> 00:21:53,576
It would include Lut(لوط) and his family who are still there.

276
00:21:54,228 --> 00:21:57,093
So he was arguing with the angels on their behalf.

277
00:21:57,834 --> 00:22:04,522
Sarah عليها السّلام when she heard the news, the first thing she thought about is the people Lut(لوط).

278
00:22:04,623 --> 00:22:05,874
 So, she laughed

279
00:22:06,932 --> 00:22:10,017
because she was happy that the punishment of Allah will come on the evil people.

280
00:22:12,145 --> 00:22:17,622
Rasool Allah ﷺ then left, so the Sahabah(صحابه) said;

281
00:22:17,646 --> 00:22:19,404
Maybe he's gonna follow the opinion of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر)

282
00:22:19,428 --> 00:22:21,309
maybe he's gonna follow the opinion of Umar(عُمَر)

283
00:22:21,549 --> 00:22:23,673
maybe it's gonna follow the opinion of Abdullah Bin Rawaha(عبدالله بن رواحة).

284
00:22:23,704 --> 00:22:24,854
Abdullah Bin Rawaha(عبدالله بن رواحة) said:

285
00:22:25,042 --> 00:22:30,662
My opinion is that you dig a trench you fill it with firewood, set it ablaze and throw them all in.

286
00:22:33,006 --> 00:22:37,268
Rasool Allah ﷺ, he came out and said: We will ransom them.

287
00:22:38,022 --> 00:22:40,630
So he followed the opinion of Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه.

288
00:22:42,142 --> 00:22:45,429
The next day, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) came

289
00:22:45,454 --> 00:22:51,309
and saw Rasool Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), sitting down and they were crying.

290
00:22:52,907 --> 00:22:55,840
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: Why are you crying? Tell me,

291
00:22:56,641 --> 00:22:59,356
because if it makes me cry; I will cry with you

292
00:22:59,381 --> 00:23:02,045
if it doesn't make me cry, I will force myself to cry.

293
00:23:02,876 --> 00:23:03,606
أتبعك

294
00:23:04,110 --> 00:23:07,721
see Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) did not want to be left out of any good.

295
00:23:08,625 --> 00:23:11,350
That's why in Makkah, when he became Muslim.

296
00:23:12,213 --> 00:23:16,819
He wanted to be like every other Muslim who is going through punishment, tormenting,

297
00:23:16,859 --> 00:23:24,081
they were all appointed to their families and tribes to persecute them, to torment them.

298
00:23:24,423 --> 00:23:27,116
Now Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب), nobody volunteered to come and torment him.

299
00:23:28,370 --> 00:23:34,107
So he was knocking on the doors trying to find somebody, so that he could be like everyone else.

300
00:23:34,401 --> 00:23:36,672
And whenever they would see Umar(عُمَر) asking for a punishment

301
00:23:36,696 --> 00:23:41,316
they close their doors, I mean who wants to torment Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) who would dare to.?

302
00:23:42,886 --> 00:23:45,453
So he wanted to be part of everything that is good.

303
00:23:46,485 --> 00:23:49,401
So he said: If I cannot cry with you, I'm gonna force myself to cry.

304
00:23:50,296 --> 00:23:56,671
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: I have seen the punishment of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ on top of that tree

305
00:23:57,307 --> 00:24:01,422
and it was about to punish my companions,

306
00:24:01,899 --> 00:24:03,883
because we have accepted to take the ransom.

307
00:24:07,115 --> 00:24:09,041
And Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ revealed the Ayaat(آيات),

308
00:24:10,084 --> 00:24:13,859
مَا كَانَ لِنَبِىٍّ أَن يَكُونَ لَهُۥٓ أَسْرَىٰ حَتَّىٰ يُثْخِنَ فِى ٱلْأَرْضِ ۚ

309
00:24:14,516 --> 00:24:17,990
تُرِيدُونَ عَرَضَ ٱلدُّنْيَا وَٱللَّهُ يُرِيدُ ٱلْآخِرَةَ

310
00:24:18,378 --> 00:24:19,846
وَٱللَّهُ عَزِيزٌ حَكِيمٌ۝

311
00:24:20,098 --> 00:24:25,234
لَّوْلَا كِتَٰبٌ مِّنَ ٱللَّهِ سَبَقَ لَمَسَّكُمْ فِيمَا أَخَذْتُمْ عَذَابٌ عَظِيمٌ۝

312
00:24:25,376 --> 00:24:30,190
فَكُلُوا مِمَّا غَنِمْتُمْ حَلَالًا طَيِّبًا ۚ وَاتَّقُوا اللَّهَ ۚ إِنَّ اللَّهَ غَفُورٌ رَحِيمٌ۝

313
00:24:30,532 --> 00:24:36,532
It is not for prophet, to have captives, until he inflicts a massacre in the land

314
00:24:36,694 --> 00:24:41,302
you desire the commodities of this world, but Allah desires for you the Hereafter.

315
00:24:41,327 --> 00:24:43,597
And Allah is Exalted in Might, and Wise.

316
00:24:44,195 --> 00:24:46,986
If not for a decree from Allah that proceeded

317
00:24:47,897 --> 00:24:52,043
you would have been touched for what you took by a great punishment.

318
00:24:52,602 --> 00:24:58,971
So consume what you have taken a war booty, as been lawful and good and fear Allah.

319
00:24:59,108 --> 00:25:01,037
Indeed, Allah is Forgiving and Merciful.

320
00:25:01,635 --> 00:25:05,488
The Ayah(آية) is saying that it was not appropriate to take captives.

321
00:25:07,125 --> 00:25:12,922
The Muslims should have killed the enemy because this was the first confrontation between Eeman(ايمان) and Kuffr(كفر).

322
00:25:14,764 --> 00:25:18,213
So Qur'an supported the opinion of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه

323
00:25:18,238 --> 00:25:22,502
and this is one of the cases where Qur'an came to confirm the opinion of Umar(عُمَر).

324
00:25:24,248 --> 00:25:32,263
And then Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says: And if it wasn't for a decree of Allah before that He would have punished you,

325
00:25:33,215 --> 00:25:35,520
The decree of Allah, some scholars say is that

326
00:25:35,560 --> 00:25:41,471
Allah has decreed that the people are Badr(بدر) there is no punishment for them that they are above punishment

327
00:25:41,506 --> 00:25:45,035
the people of Badr(بدر) the ones who were there at that decisive moment

328
00:25:45,559 --> 00:25:47,004
because that was a special day.

329
00:25:47,746 --> 00:25:50,696
Later on Jibreel عليه السّلام came to Muhammadﷺ and said:

330
00:25:50,950 --> 00:25:53,348
What do you consider the people of Badr(بدر) to be among you?

331
00:25:53,774 --> 00:25:56,756
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: We consider them to be the best among us.

332
00:25:56,979 --> 00:25:58,441
Jibreel عليه السّلام said:

333
00:25:58,629 --> 00:26:03,535
And the angels consider the angels who attended the Battle of Badr(بدر) to be the best among the angels.

334
00:26:03,822 --> 00:26:07,353
So it's not only the best among humans but it's also the best among angels.

335
00:26:07,786 --> 00:26:12,890
That was a day that was witnessed by the creation of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ in the above world

336
00:26:13,310 --> 00:26:16,548
the Higher World of the angels, this was a special day.

337
00:26:17,402 --> 00:26:20,528
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ has granted the people of Badr(بدر), forgiveness

338
00:26:20,552 --> 00:26:22,098
and that's why he didn't punish them.

339
00:26:22,993 --> 00:26:25,829
Another opinion is that the reason why the punishment did not come

340
00:26:26,130 --> 00:26:32,312
is that Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ has made it, Halal(حلال) for Rasool Allah ﷺ and the Sahabah(صحابه) to take booty of war.

341
00:26:32,572 --> 00:26:34,488
 In another Hadith(حديث) Rasool Allah ﷺ says:

342
00:26:34,734 --> 00:26:36,867
Five things were made Halal(حلال) for me

343
00:26:36,891 --> 00:26:39,734
and they have never been made Halal(حلال) for prophet before me.

344
00:26:40,801 --> 00:26:41,471
Number one,

345
00:26:42,577 --> 00:26:44,810
نُصرتُ بِرُعْبِ نصيرة الشَّهر

346
00:26:44,834 --> 00:26:46,913
Rasool Allah ﷺ says: I was given five things

347
00:26:47,144 --> 00:26:49,125
that will never given to a prophet before me.

348
00:26:49,348 --> 00:26:55,512
Number one, I was assisted with fear, a distance of a month.

349
00:26:55,992 --> 00:27:00,481
Meaning, Rasool Allah ﷺ would start marching towards an enemy

350
00:27:01,524 --> 00:27:06,906
the enemy would be terrified even if the enemy is 30 days away from Rasool Allah ﷺ.

351
00:27:08,104 --> 00:27:08,889
Number two,

352
00:27:08,913 --> 00:27:14,776
جُعِلَ فِى الأرض لي مسجدًا وطهورًا، فَأيُّمَا في رجلٍ أمَّتي أدركته’ صلاة فيصلِّي

353
00:27:15,326 --> 00:27:18,518
The whole land the whole earth was made a Masjid(مسجد) for me.

354
00:27:18,803 --> 00:27:20,593
therefore, pray wherever you can.

355
00:27:21,800 --> 00:27:26,873
See what the other Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) and their followers they had to pray in the worship places

356
00:27:27,177 --> 00:27:31,906
but with the Ummah(امة) of Muhammadﷺ, Allah has made the whole earth a Masjid(مسجد), you can pray wherever.

357
00:27:32,310 --> 00:27:37,170
 Therefore, any piece of land is Taher(طاهر)

358
00:27:37,494 --> 00:27:40,441
you assume that it is Taher(طاهر), unless you see Najaasa(نجاسه) on it.

359
00:27:42,327 --> 00:27:44,739
ألاصل في الأمور ألطهارة

360
00:27:44,763 --> 00:27:48,063
That it is the original status of something is that it is Taher(طاهر).

361
00:27:48,096 --> 00:27:49,898
ولا يزول اليقين بشك

362
00:27:50,348 --> 00:27:57,494
And if it is certain that it is Taher(طاهر) that certainty cannot be shaken by doubt, you have to see Najaasa(نجاسه) on it,

363
00:27:57,787 --> 00:27:59,498
 therefore you can pray in the parks

364
00:27:59,729 --> 00:28:02,168
you can pray on the pavement, you can pray in the mall

365
00:28:02,192 --> 00:28:04,432
you can pray in the airport, you can play anywhere.

366
00:28:04,632 --> 00:28:09,589
And you assume that this is clean and Taher(طاهر) unless you can actually see a Najaasa(نجاسه).

367
00:28:10,148 --> 00:28:14,019
And the way you know the Najaasa(نجاسه) is by the smell, or the sight of it

368
00:28:14,516 --> 00:28:17,817
otherwise you assume that it is clean, Taher(طاهر).

369
00:28:18,407 --> 00:28:21,980
Because there's a lot of Waswasah(وسوسه) that happens in the Tahara(طهارة) aspect

370
00:28:22,114 --> 00:28:25,815
people have a lots of waswasah(وسوسه) and that's from Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ), so that's number two.

371
00:28:25,839 --> 00:28:26,526
Number three,

372
00:28:27,694 --> 00:28:28,977
أحلَّت ليَّ الْغنائم

373
00:28:30,458 --> 00:28:33,319
The booty of war was made Halal(حلال) for me.

374
00:28:34,534 --> 00:28:39,014
All of the other Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) they were not allowed to take the booty of war.

375
00:28:39,556 --> 00:28:42,246
For example, with Bannu Israel(بنواسرائيل), they had to gather it and burn it

376
00:28:42,332 --> 00:28:44,629
but for Muhammadﷺ it was made Halal(حلال)

377
00:28:45,152 --> 00:28:46,705
and Rasool Allah ﷺ in fact says:

378
00:28:46,736 --> 00:28:48,400
جُعِلَ رزقي تحت ظل رمحي

379
00:28:48,646 --> 00:28:52,593
My Rizq(رزق), my sustenance, comes from beneath my spear.

380
00:28:53,996 --> 00:28:57,362
And the Sahabah(صحابه) used to consider the most Halal(حلال) form of Rizq(رزق)

381
00:28:57,386 --> 00:28:58,231
 is the booty of war.

382
00:29:01,431 --> 00:29:02,378
The fourth,

383
00:29:03,813 --> 00:29:04,447
the intercession

384
00:29:04,471 --> 00:29:05,586
أحلَّت لي شفاعة

385
00:29:05,902 --> 00:29:09,258
The intercession, now there's minor Shafaa(شفاعة)

386
00:29:09,283 --> 00:29:10,515
and there's greater Shafaa(شفاعة).

387
00:29:10,996 --> 00:29:14,418
The great Shafaa(شفاعة), Shafaa Al-Uzma(شفاع العظمى) is only given to Muhammadﷺ.

388
00:29:14,813 --> 00:29:18,369
The minor Shafaa(شفاعة), Shafaa-As-Sughra(شفاعة الصغرة) can be given to the other Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء)

389
00:29:18,592 --> 00:29:22,662
it's also given to the Shuhada(شهداء), and it can be given to the some Saliheen(صالحين) from this Ummah(امة)

390
00:29:22,894 --> 00:29:24,334
so that's the Shafaa(شفاعة).

391
00:29:24,554 --> 00:29:28,582
And the final one that I was sent to all mankind,

392
00:29:29,078 --> 00:29:31,992
while all of the other prophets were sent to their particular people.

393
00:29:33,012 --> 00:29:37,026
أرْسِلْتُ على الناس عامة، وكل كان نبي أرسل الى قو مه الخاصه

394
00:29:37,406 --> 00:29:41,263
So these five things are five special, unique qualities

395
00:29:41,517 --> 00:29:43,346
that were given to Muhammadﷺ.

396
00:29:46,468 --> 00:29:48,379
So that's Battle of Badr(بدر), in the Battle of Uhud(أحَد)

397
00:29:49,031 --> 00:29:50,446
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه says:

398
00:29:50,471 --> 00:29:54,538
When we retreated, I was the first one to go back to Rasool Allah ﷺ.

399
00:29:55,003 --> 00:29:56,659
He was the first to go back,

400
00:29:56,751 --> 00:30:03,128
Rasool Allah ﷺ and the Sahabah(صحابه), they were hiding in a crevice in the mountain of Uhud(أحَد),

401
00:30:03,756 --> 00:30:05,225
Shu'ab(شعب), a valley.

402
00:30:07,307 --> 00:30:10,775
And that's how Rasool Allah ﷺ protected the Sahabah(صحابه) from the advancing army

403
00:30:10,815 --> 00:30:12,687
he went up the mountain of Uhud(أحَد).

404
00:30:12,981 --> 00:30:15,245
So the Kuffar(كفار) failed to pursue them.

405
00:30:15,913 --> 00:30:21,653
So Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان) came under the, mountain, under the place where the Sahabah(صحابه) were hiding, and he said:

406
00:30:21,779 --> 00:30:23,190
أفي القومي محمد؟

407
00:30:23,975 --> 00:30:26,335
Is a Muhammad(محمد) among you صلى الله عليه وسلم?"

408
00:30:28,140 --> 00:30:30,147
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: "Do not answer him".

409
00:30:31,964 --> 00:30:34,678
أفي القومي أبا بكر؟

410
00:30:35,636 --> 00:30:37,260
Is Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) among you?

411
00:30:39,139 --> 00:30:40,302
Rasool Ullah said: "Don't answer him".

412
00:30:40,791 --> 00:30:41,231
And then he said:

413
00:30:41,255 --> 00:30:42,637
أفي القومي عمر؟

414
00:30:43,274 --> 00:30:44,797
Is Umar(عُمَر) among you?

415
00:30:44,822 --> 00:30:48,982
Later on Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب), he stood up and said:

416
00:30:49,721 --> 00:30:52,248
All of the three, whom you mentioned are alive

417
00:30:53,400 --> 00:30:56,653
 and Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ has made them alive to anger you and your people.

418
00:30:58,852 --> 00:31:02,403
The reason, why I'm mentioning this conversation or incident

419
00:31:03,157 --> 00:31:06,359
is to show you that Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان) only asked about three people.

420
00:31:07,488 --> 00:31:10,079
He asked about Rasool Allah ﷺ, he asked about Abu Bakr(ابوبكر),

421
00:31:10,103 --> 00:31:11,126
and he asked about Umar(عُمَر)

422
00:31:12,817 --> 00:31:17,831
because they were viewed as the leaders of the community of the Muslims.

423
00:31:18,077 --> 00:31:23,427
Rasool Allah ﷺ, and his two advisors Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and Umar رضي الله عنهما.

424
00:31:25,098 --> 00:31:28,674
We move on to Sulhal-Hudaybiyaa(صلح الحديبية).

425
00:31:30,709 --> 00:31:33,262
Sulhal-Hudaybiyaa(صلح الحديبية) was the truce, the peace agreement

426
00:31:33,286 --> 00:31:38,672
that occurred between Rasool Allah ﷺ and the Mushrikeen(مشركين) of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ)

427
00:31:39,410 --> 00:31:40,551
after years of battle.

428
00:31:40,575 --> 00:31:43,679
This happened in the six year of Hijrah(هجرة)

429
00:31:44,535 --> 00:31:50,464
So Badr(بدر) was in the second, Uhud(أحَد) was the third, Al-Khandaq(ألخندق) was the fifth

430
00:31:50,980 --> 00:31:54,043
and then Hudaybiyaa(حديبية) happened in the sixth year of Hijrah(هجرة).

431
00:31:56,535 --> 00:32:04,734
The people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) sent one delegate after another to bargain a deal with Muhammadﷺ.

432
00:32:04,974 --> 00:32:11,044
Muhammadﷺ and the Sahabah(صحابه) came to Makkah with the intention of making Umrah(عمرة).

433
00:32:11,493 --> 00:32:15,283
The people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) did not want to allow them in. They said:

434
00:32:15,307 --> 00:32:16,451
لا إخلا علينا عنوة

435
00:32:16,681 --> 00:32:18,784
We're not gonna allow him to come in, by force.

436
00:32:19,796 --> 00:32:22,840
So they were insisting on negotiating with Muhammadﷺ

437
00:32:22,864 --> 00:32:25,192
and this is the first time Muhammadﷺ negotiates with them.

438
00:32:26,602 --> 00:32:28,625
So they send one delegate after another

439
00:32:29,762 --> 00:32:32,566
they sent Urawa Bin Masood As-Saqafi(عروةبن مسعود ألثقفي).

440
00:32:33,547 --> 00:32:36,069
Who was from Banu Saqeef(بنوثقيف) in At-Taef(اَلطَّائِف),

441
00:32:37,479 --> 00:32:40,800
he came, and he's not from Makkah, he's from a different tribe.

442
00:32:41,562 --> 00:32:45,240
He comes, takes a look at Rasool Allah ﷺ and the Sahabah(صحابه)

443
00:32:45,884 --> 00:32:51,341
and he says: "The people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) have came out with their women and their children.

444
00:32:52,832 --> 00:32:58,832
And they came out dressed in the skins of lions prepared for war,

445
00:33:00,446 --> 00:33:02,378
and they are not going to allow you in.

446
00:33:03,228 --> 00:33:08,402
And O Muhammad(محمد) you have gathered around you OBaash An-Naas(أوباش الناس), the scum of the earth.

447
00:33:10,906 --> 00:33:16,220
So I can only assume that they will run away from you, and desert you

448
00:33:17,146 --> 00:33:22,202
and he said: You have gathered around you the scum of the earth to go and fight the noble people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ),

449
00:33:22,337 --> 00:33:23,397
 very insulting words.

450
00:33:25,182 --> 00:33:28,049
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه responded by a statement,

451
00:33:28,577 --> 00:33:31,387
 and if you can't stand the statement, Close your ears.

452
00:33:32,001 --> 00:33:38,903
He said: Go and suck on the clitoris of Al-Laat(ألَّات), very strong statement.

453
00:33:41,200 --> 00:33:47,260
Al-Laat(ألَّات) is a goddess, that the people of the Saqeef(ثقيف) had in At-Taef(اَلطَّائِف).

454
00:33:48,875 --> 00:33:52,784
It was a goddess, it was female, so it was very insulting statement.

455
00:33:54,688 --> 00:34:02,050
Now, before mentioning this I have debated whether I should go ahead and mention this incident, or forget about it.

456
00:34:02,875 --> 00:34:06,224
But then I came to the decision that I should mention it

457
00:34:06,902 --> 00:34:10,573
because first of all it's in the Al-Bukhari(بخاريْ), we cannot deny the authenticity of it.

458
00:34:11,398 --> 00:34:14,900
And second of all, I see that there's a lot, that you can learn from this incident

459
00:34:15,677 --> 00:34:20,740
because it tells you something about the personality of Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه in particular,

460
00:34:20,923 --> 00:34:23,268
 and something about the Sahabah(صحابه), in general.

461
00:34:25,459 --> 00:34:30,101
Ibn Hajar Asqalani(إبن حجرألعسقلاني), because he gave a commentary on the Bukhari(بخاريْ)

462
00:34:30,352 --> 00:34:34,066
and he can't skip this event without commenting on it.

463
00:34:35,469 --> 00:34:42,224
He says, that this curse was a curse that was known among the Arabs

464
00:34:42,248 --> 00:34:46,636
but they used to use the mother instead of Al-Laat(ألَّات), in that curse.

465
00:34:47,722 --> 00:34:50,718
Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) replaced it with Al-Laat(ألَّات), a goddess

466
00:34:50,742 --> 00:34:52,519
 that the people of Saqeef(ثقيف) used to worship.

467
00:34:54,366 --> 00:35:00,015
Now, one might wonder why would Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه used such an obscene word.

468
00:35:02,019 --> 00:35:05,312
When I thought about this and I've read this incident years ago,

469
00:35:05,352 --> 00:35:07,662
 I mean in the beginning, it could be a bit surprised

470
00:35:08,494 --> 00:35:14,472
but when you think about it and you put it into perspective you appreciate what happened.

471
00:35:15,480 --> 00:35:22,311
You see the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم had a certain love of Rasool Allah ﷺ that we cannot comprehend.

472
00:35:23,339 --> 00:35:32,157
It was at a certain level that we can sometimes when we read these stories we don't understand, what is going on.

473
00:35:32,724 --> 00:35:38,684
The statement of Urwa Bin Masood(عروة بن مسعود) was an insult to Muhammadﷺ.

474
00:35:39,891 --> 00:35:44,299
He said: "You've gathered around you the scum of the people to attack the noble people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

475
00:35:44,543 --> 00:35:50,816
So first of all, he's implying that these are lowly people attacking the best of the people.

476
00:35:51,250 --> 00:35:56,540
And it's also implying that Rasool Allah ﷺ and his mission is a failure.

477
00:35:57,661 --> 00:36:01,859
When you say that the people around Muhammadﷺ are Obaash(أوباش).

478
00:36:03,063 --> 00:36:05,890
In other words you're saying that the Rasool Allah ﷺ has failed in his mission

479
00:36:06,277 --> 00:36:11,198
because the scholar is who, his students are, and you are, who your friends are.

480
00:36:12,265 --> 00:36:18,258
So anybody who speaks against Sahabah رضي الله عنهم is accusing Muhammadﷺ in failing in his mission

481
00:36:18,643 --> 00:36:22,878
because the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم, are the product of the Da'wah(دعوة) of Rasool Allah ﷺ

482
00:36:23,875 --> 00:36:26,729
they were the harvest of the seeds that he planted.

483
00:36:27,929 --> 00:36:31,261
So an attack on the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم, is an attack on him.

484
00:36:32,305 --> 00:36:37,677
The Sahabah رضي الله عنهم cannot handle seeing anyone insulting Rasool Allah ﷺ

485
00:36:38,001 --> 00:36:39,231
they cannot tolerate that.

486
00:36:40,281 --> 00:36:42,738
To give you an illustrate of some other examples

487
00:36:43,266 --> 00:36:47,892
While Marwan Bin Hakam(مروان بن حكم) was the governor of Madina in the time of Al-Khilafah Al-Amwiyah(خلافه ألأموية).

488
00:36:49,155 --> 00:36:54,155
He was in the gathering, and there was Bin Yameen Al-Yahudi(بنيامين أليهودي)  a Jew called Bin Yameen(بن يامين).

489
00:36:54,206 --> 00:36:57,083
I assume at that time he was a Muslim because this happened in Madina.

490
00:36:57,645 --> 00:36:59,064
He could be Allah Ho Alam(الله أعلم).

491
00:36:59,620 --> 00:37:04,890
And Muhammad Bin Maslamah(محمد بن مسلمة), by that time was an old man and he was also in that meeting.

492
00:37:05,334 --> 00:37:08,507
Marwan Bin Hakam(مروان بن حكم) asked Bin Yameen(بن يامين) what do you consider

493
00:37:08,754 --> 00:37:12,839
what's your opinion about the assassination of Ka'ab Ibn Al-Ashraf(كعب إبن ألأشرف)?

494
00:37:13,844 --> 00:37:18,011
Kaab Ibn Al-Ashraf(كعب إبن ألأشرف) was a Jewish leader in Arabia

495
00:37:18,571 --> 00:37:22,015
who had his own fortress, close to Madina

496
00:37:23,031 --> 00:37:28,699
and he was one of the mobilizers of the effort to distort and fight Islam

497
00:37:29,072 --> 00:37:32,300
and he used all of his resources for that purpose, his wealth.

498
00:37:32,655 --> 00:37:37,029
And he was a very great poet, and he was the one behind the scene

499
00:37:37,338 --> 00:37:40,992
mobilizing the Arabs and the Jews to fight Muhammadﷺ

500
00:37:42,535 --> 00:37:44,101
he started crossing the red line.

501
00:37:45,098 --> 00:37:50,002
He was making poetry, in which he was describing the women of Sahabah(صحابه).

502
00:37:50,744 --> 00:37:54,400
So Rasool Allah ﷺ to defend the honor of the women of the Sahabah(صحابه) said:

503
00:37:54,424 --> 00:37:57,270
منْ لِّي بكعب إبن أشرف فإنه’ فأذ الله ورسوله

504
00:37:57,719 --> 00:37:59,349
Who will take care of Ka'ab Ibn Al-Ashraf(كعب إبن ألأشرف)

505
00:37:59,373 --> 00:38:01,038
because he has harmed Allah and His messenger.

506
00:38:01,893 --> 00:38:04,204
Muhammad Bin Maslamah(محمد بن مسلمة) volunteered, he said: I will!

507
00:38:04,638 --> 00:38:08,891
So Rasool Allah ﷺ agreed to appoint him to this Special Operation mission

508
00:38:09,340 --> 00:38:11,245
to go and assassinate Ka'ab Ibn Al-Ashraf(كعب إبن ألأشرف)

509
00:38:11,829 --> 00:38:13,489
and he went along with five Sahabah(صحابه).

510
00:38:14,929 --> 00:38:17,352
Anyway, I'm not going to go into the details of what happened.

511
00:38:17,997 --> 00:38:20,232
He was assassinated by these five men.

512
00:38:21,126 --> 00:38:23,082
When Marwan Bin Hakam(مروان بن حكم) asked Bin Yameen(بن يامين),

513
00:38:23,107 --> 00:38:24,644
"What's your view about this?

514
00:38:24,684 --> 00:38:26,692
Bin Yameen(بن يامين) said: I think it's treachery.

515
00:38:29,253 --> 00:38:35,306
Now he's accusing the Sahabah(صحابه) who did this, by being treacherous.

516
00:38:37,677 --> 00:38:41,551
But Muhammad Bin Maslamah(محمد بن مسلمة) considers this to be an attack on Rasool Allah ﷺ.

517
00:38:41,591 --> 00:38:45,825
 He said: The one, who ordered us to do that was Rasool Allah ﷺ

518
00:38:46,993 --> 00:38:49,298
and then he told Marwan Bin Hakam(مروان بن حكم),

519
00:38:49,427 --> 00:38:50,869
أيُغدر رسول الله

520
00:38:52,397 --> 00:38:58,231
Can we accuse Rasool Allah ﷺ of treachery and you are quiet, you do nothing about it".

521
00:38:58,969 --> 00:39:00,375
 And then he told Bin Yameen(بن يامين),

522
00:39:00,988 --> 00:39:05,631
"If I ever see you and I have my sword with me, I'm going to make you leave without your head.

523
00:39:07,267 --> 00:39:11,027
And Muhammad Bin Maslamah(محمد بن مسلمة) was a very feeble old man at that time

524
00:39:11,383 --> 00:39:12,199
very old.

525
00:39:13,906 --> 00:39:18,132
The narrator of this story says: Bin Yameen(بن يامين) would never leave his home

526
00:39:18,660 --> 00:39:21,370
unless he knows that Muhammad Bin Maslamah(محمد بن مسلمة) is nowhere in the vicinity

527
00:39:22,039 --> 00:39:22,919
he's nowhere around.

528
00:39:23,962 --> 00:39:27,618
However, one day, the Qadar(قَدَر) of Allah brought them together in the cemetery.

529
00:39:28,184 --> 00:39:31,475
So Muhammad Bin Maslamah(محمد بن مسلمة) did not have any weapons with him.

530
00:39:32,033 --> 00:39:34,611
He picked up whatever he could from the ground, sticks

531
00:39:35,279 --> 00:39:39,350
and he went to beat Bin Yameen(بن يامين) until he left him motionless and he told him:

532
00:39:39,374 --> 00:39:42,078
If I had my sword with me, I would have beheaded you.

533
00:39:44,996 --> 00:39:48,095
The Sahabah رضي الله عنهم, did not tolerate insulting Rasool Allah ﷺ

534
00:39:48,120 --> 00:39:51,173
to give you another story, which is more dramatic.

535
00:39:52,482 --> 00:39:55,053
And this is a story that some people might not understand

536
00:39:55,077 --> 00:39:56,601
and the ones, who would not understand

537
00:39:56,641 --> 00:40:01,884
these are the ones who do not appreciate the level of the love that the Sahabah(صحابه) had to Muhammadﷺ.

538
00:40:03,607 --> 00:40:09,394
This was a blind man in Madina, his wife, whom he loves very much

539
00:40:10,171 --> 00:40:14,301
used to from time to time, speak negatively about Muhammadﷺ,

540
00:40:15,438 --> 00:40:19,414
she would insult him, talk negatively about him, blame him

541
00:40:20,285 --> 00:40:22,101
and her husband would always tell her:

542
00:40:22,239 --> 00:40:26,537
My wife don't speak against Muhammadﷺ, stop that.! Don't do it again.

543
00:40:27,916 --> 00:40:29,802
And she would keep on doing it again and again.

544
00:40:30,806 --> 00:40:34,755
One day he got fed up, he took a dagger and he stabbed her to death

545
00:40:36,274 --> 00:40:37,841
and this is in Sunan Abi Dawood(سنن أبي داؤد).

546
00:40:39,220 --> 00:40:41,850
The next day they find this dead body and

547
00:40:42,492 --> 00:40:44,857
Rasool Allah ﷺ gathers the Sahabah(صحابه) and says:

548
00:40:45,056 --> 00:40:50,589
"Whoever sees that it is his duty to obey me, Come and speak."

549
00:40:51,317 --> 00:40:54,442
And Rasool Allah ﷺ wants to know who committed this crime. He said:

550
00:40:54,726 --> 00:41:00,015
Whoever sees that he has a right towards me, come and tell me who killed this woman?

551
00:41:01,768 --> 00:41:06,098
So the narrator of the Hadith(حديث) says the blind man stood up and he was shaking, trembling.

552
00:41:06,976 --> 00:41:10,048
And he came to Rasool Allah ﷺ and he was very afraid, terrified.

553
00:41:10,654 --> 00:41:12,552
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Why did you do that?

554
00:41:13,728 --> 00:41:14,784
He said: O Messenger of Allah

555
00:41:14,808 --> 00:41:15,843
كان تقه فيك

556
00:41:16,191 --> 00:41:18,001
She used to speak ill about you.

557
00:41:18,557 --> 00:41:21,224
And I told her again and again to stop but she refused.

558
00:41:21,791 --> 00:41:23,049
And that's why I killed her.

559
00:41:23,702 --> 00:41:24,896
Rasool Allah ﷺ said:

560
00:41:25,494 --> 00:41:26,918
فَاِنَّ دَمَّھا حضر

561
00:41:27,266 --> 00:41:33,272
Her blood is waste you don't have to pay any blood money and you're not punished for that sin

562
00:41:33,906 --> 00:41:36,451
if that's why you killed her!

563
00:41:36,674 --> 00:41:37,607
فَدَمُھا حضر

564
00:41:39,033 --> 00:41:43,879
Now, again this is a story that some people might not appreciate and they would think that, this is brutality.

565
00:41:44,783 --> 00:41:51,099
But for someone who understands that the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم were so involved in their love towards Rasool Allah ﷺ

566
00:41:51,139 --> 00:41:55,340
they were willing to sacrifice anything and everything for him, this is normal.

567
00:41:57,063 --> 00:42:00,586
So when Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه uses such words.

568
00:42:01,098 --> 00:42:08,824
That was because he was very angry, and cannot tolerate seeing Rasool Allah ﷺ being insulted in such a manner,

569
00:42:10,046 --> 00:42:12,125
 that wasn't the character of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

570
00:42:12,316 --> 00:42:18,311
Those weren't words of Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه would usually use that was a once in a lifetime thing.

571
00:42:18,494 --> 00:42:21,161
And it only came out in defense of Rasool Allah ﷺ

572
00:42:21,486 --> 00:42:26,265
and if Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه was insulted he would never respond in such a way.

573
00:42:26,918 --> 00:42:30,380
But because it was an insult towards Rasool Allah ﷺ

574
00:42:30,720 --> 00:42:32,641
he dealt with it in a different fashion and way.

575
00:42:33,379 --> 00:42:39,253
So Ibn Hajar Asqalani(إبن حجرألعسقلاني) says that this is not considered to be fahsh(فحش) it's not considered to be obscenity,

576
00:42:39,507 --> 00:42:45,857
 because Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه did it to stop somebody who was cursing Rasool Allah ﷺ.

577
00:42:45,897 --> 00:42:52,718
 And he said: It is allowed therefore in such situations, to use words that should not be used

578
00:42:52,895 --> 00:43:00,059
if it's going to stop and aggression against Islam, and the figure of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

579
00:43:01,939 --> 00:43:05,437
So I hope now you understand why this happened,

580
00:43:05,754 --> 00:43:08,212
and you put it in the right perspective.

581
00:43:09,961 --> 00:43:12,321
By the way when Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) insulted him in such a way

582
00:43:12,645 --> 00:43:16,463
I mean this was an insult to their god or goddess, he said:

583
00:43:16,974 --> 00:43:20,885
You have done me a favor and if it wasn't for your favor on me,

584
00:43:21,131 --> 00:43:22,360
I would have responded to you.

585
00:43:23,700 --> 00:43:27,808
So look at the favors of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) have reached everyone even somebody in At-Taef(اَلطَّائِف).

586
00:43:28,642 --> 00:43:32,126
Rasool Allah ﷺ has done people so many favors, Muslim and Non Muslim.

587
00:43:33,076 --> 00:43:36,285
So Urwa Bin Masood(عُروة بن مسعود) said: If it wasn't for your favors upon me

588
00:43:36,437 --> 00:43:38,026
I would have responded to you appropriately.

589
00:43:41,420 --> 00:43:44,636
I think it was Urwa Bin Masood(عُروة بن مسعود), went back to Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) and said:

590
00:43:45,750 --> 00:43:50,241
O people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), I have visited an Najashi(نجاشي) in his palace

591
00:43:51,214 --> 00:43:55,165
and I have visited Heracules in his palace, Heracul(هراقل)

592
00:43:56,403 --> 00:44:00,955
the Roman Emperor and I visited Kisra(كسرى) in his palace

593
00:44:01,334 --> 00:44:07,407
I have never in my life seen people, who respect their leader and love him so much

594
00:44:07,582 --> 00:44:09,464
and are willing to give their lives for him,

595
00:44:09,759 --> 00:44:12,963
like the followers of Muhammadﷺ, treat Muhammadﷺ.

596
00:44:14,765 --> 00:44:20,867
I have visited the courts of the kings around the world, and I've seen them.

597
00:44:21,653 --> 00:44:27,233
But I have never a seen a people who respect their leader as much as the Sahabah(صحابه) respect Muhammadﷺ.

598
00:44:27,471 --> 00:44:28,907
So he did learn a lesson from that.

599
00:44:32,378 --> 00:44:37,717
Rasool Allah ﷺ would receive one delegate after another and then in the end they sent Sohail Ibn Amr(سهيل إبن عمرو),

600
00:44:38,201 --> 00:44:42,149
 who succeeded in signing an agreement with Muhammadﷺ

601
00:44:43,138 --> 00:44:46,110
the Muslims were not happy with the agreement,

602
00:44:47,306 --> 00:44:49,682
because they didn't see the wisdom behind it.

603
00:44:52,064 --> 00:44:53,775
And this was the prevalent view

604
00:44:54,912 --> 00:44:57,566
the Muslims were unhappy with that agreement

605
00:44:58,437 --> 00:44:59,781
and they wish that it never happened.

606
00:45:00,638 --> 00:45:04,149
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) being the outspoken one among the Sahabah(صحابه)

607
00:45:04,499 --> 00:45:06,262
he went to Rasool Allah ﷺ and he said:

608
00:45:06,672 --> 00:45:09,644
O Messenger of Allah! Aren't you the Messenger of Allah?

609
00:45:09,828 --> 00:45:13,192
He said: Yes!. Aren't we the Muslims? He said: Yes!

610
00:45:13,610 --> 00:45:16,546
Aren't they, the disbelievers? He said: Yes!

611
00:45:17,659 --> 00:45:21,735
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: Then why should we negotiate with them in such an agreement?

612
00:45:22,733 --> 00:45:28,386
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: I am the messenger of Allah, and I'm not going to disobey His command.

613
00:45:29,112 --> 00:45:31,459
And then Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said, O messenger of Allah!

614
00:45:31,499 --> 00:45:34,415
Didnt u tell us that we're gonna visit Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه)"?

615
00:45:35,755 --> 00:45:39,323
They've miss Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه) so much, they've been away from Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه) for six years now.

616
00:45:39,809 --> 00:45:44,011
And Rasool Allah ﷺ has promised them that they're gonna make Tawaf(طواف) around Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه),

617
00:45:44,114 --> 00:45:49,217
because part of the agreement is that you don't go to Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه) now you come back next year.

618
00:45:49,595 --> 00:45:53,405
Umar(عُمَر) said: O Messenger of Allah, didn't you promised us that we would visit Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه)?

619
00:45:53,603 --> 00:45:56,036
 Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Yes! I did promise you that.

620
00:45:56,283 --> 00:45:58,233
But did I tell you, it's going to be this year.

621
00:45:59,010 --> 00:45:59,861
Umar(عُمَر) said: No!

622
00:46:00,034 --> 00:46:04,143
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Then you will visit it and you will make the Tawaf(طواف) around it.

623
00:46:04,808 --> 00:46:06,231
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) went to Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

624
00:46:06,892 --> 00:46:08,811
He said: Isn't he the Messenger of Allah? He sais: Yes

625
00:46:09,003 --> 00:46:10,282
Aren't we the Muslims?, Yes!

626
00:46:10,481 --> 00:46:11,730
Aren't these the Kuffar(كفار)?, Yes!

627
00:46:11,871 --> 00:46:15,194
why should we negotiate with them on such terms?

628
00:46:16,651 --> 00:46:18,433
Abu Bakr Siddique رضي الله عنه said:

629
00:46:18,600 --> 00:46:20,017
إلزم غُرزة

630
00:46:21,192 --> 00:46:26,479
Al-Ghurz(غُرز) is the stirrup of the horse, when you ride the horse you put your feet in the stirrup.

631
00:46:27,400 --> 00:46:30,378
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) said: Stick to the stirrup of Rasool Allah ﷺ

632
00:46:30,597 --> 00:46:32,397
means follow him wherever he goes

633
00:46:34,425 --> 00:46:35,705
فَإ نَّه’ رسول الله

634
00:46:35,897 --> 00:46:38,789
He is a messenger of Allah and He will never disobey Allah

635
00:46:38,887 --> 00:46:41,019
and Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ will never forsake Him.

636
00:46:41,527 --> 00:46:42,654
Allah will be on his side.

637
00:46:43,047 --> 00:46:45,883
Therefore, stick with whatever Rasool Allah ﷺ does.

638
00:46:46,434 --> 00:46:48,307
Therefore the Scholars commented on that,

639
00:46:48,465 --> 00:46:53,386
and they say that As Siddique(ألصديق) always was at a higher status than the rest of the Sahabah(صحابه).

640
00:46:54,198 --> 00:46:58,478
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه would later on comment on Sulhal Hudaybiyyah(صلح الحديبيه)

641
00:46:59,021 --> 00:47:02,003
again the Sahabah(صحابه) saw this as a loss

642
00:47:03,718 --> 00:47:05,843
when in reality it was victory for them.

643
00:47:07,488 --> 00:47:10,447
And Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه not only considers it to be victory.

644
00:47:10,471 --> 00:47:13,709
He said: I consider it to be the greatest victory in Islam,

645
00:47:14,088 --> 00:47:14,987
 Sulhal Hudaybiyyah(صلح الحديبيه).

646
00:47:16,881 --> 00:47:19,062
Listen to the words of Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) he says:

647
00:47:19,087 --> 00:47:28,611
ما كان فتحٌ أعظم في الإسلام من فتح ألحديبيه ولكن الناس قَصُرَ رءيَّهُم عمًّا كان بين محمد وربَّ

648
00:47:29,311 --> 00:47:34,695
والْعبادُ يعجلون والله لا يعجل كعجلةِ العباد حتى يبلغ الأمور ما أراد

649
00:47:35,188 --> 00:47:39,614
There was no opening greater in the history of Islam than the opening of Hudaybiyyah(حديبية)

650
00:47:40,111 --> 00:47:42,332
but people are short sighted

651
00:47:43,250 --> 00:47:47,517
and they did not know what was going on between Allah and Muhammadﷺ.

652
00:47:48,061 --> 00:47:51,418
There was something going on between Allah and Muhammadﷺ in Sulhal Hudaybiyyah(صلح الحديبيه)

653
00:47:51,616 --> 00:47:53,012
 that the Sahabah(صحابه) did not know

654
00:47:53,758 --> 00:47:55,751
Qasura Rayahum(قصُرَرَايئهم) they were short sighted.

655
00:47:56,599 --> 00:48:00,634
And then he says, and the nature of people is that they hasten things

656
00:48:00,927 --> 00:48:04,527
but the Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ does not Hasten things, until they are completed

657
00:48:05,430 --> 00:48:08,263
Allah has His Qadar(قَدَر) and it works in a certain way,

658
00:48:08,550 --> 00:48:10,248
people want things to come fast.

659
00:48:11,775 --> 00:48:15,695
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), I will continue with the statement of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) the translation of it.

660
00:48:18,740 --> 00:48:25,157
Rasool Allah ﷺ and Suhail(سهيل) were agreeing on the terms and Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) was one, writing them down.

661
00:48:25,746 --> 00:48:29,084
So Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Write down! He said Ali(علي) to Write down

662
00:48:29,108 --> 00:48:30,472
بسم الله الرحمن الرحيم

663
00:48:30,703 --> 00:48:33,189
In the Name of Allah, the Merciful, the Beneficent.

664
00:48:33,670 --> 00:48:34,931
Suhail Ibn Amr(سهيل إبن عمرو) said: No,

665
00:48:35,646 --> 00:48:38,182
We do not know Ar-Rahman(ألرحمن), Ar-Rahim(الرحيم) we know Allah.

666
00:48:38,624 --> 00:48:40,130
We don't know Ar-Rahman(ألرحمن), Ar-Rahim(الرحيم).

667
00:48:40,369 --> 00:48:42,800
Therefore write Bismika Allah-Humm(بسمك الله هم), in the name of Allah

668
00:48:44,382 --> 00:48:46,053
Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) refused to erase that

669
00:48:46,077 --> 00:48:47,508
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him Erase it.

670
00:48:49,340 --> 00:48:50,510
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ said:

671
00:48:50,534 --> 00:48:53,641
هذا ما صالح عليه محمد رسول الله

672
00:48:53,997 --> 00:48:58,123
This is what Muhammad(محمد), the Messenger of Allah, agreed upon

673
00:48:58,666 --> 00:49:00,984
Suhail Ibn Amr(سهيل إبن عمرو) interrupted and said: No,

674
00:49:02,145 --> 00:49:04,507
If we agree that you are the Messenger of Allah.

675
00:49:04,531 --> 00:49:06,119
We wouldn't have been negotiating with you.

676
00:49:07,441 --> 00:49:10,709
The whole issue between us and you is that we do not agree

677
00:49:11,198 --> 00:49:14,125
we do not approve that you are the messenger of Allah.

678
00:49:14,379 --> 00:49:17,021
So we told Ali(علي) to erase that Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) refused.

679
00:49:17,728 --> 00:49:19,516
Rasool Allah ﷺ told Ali(علي) to erase it

680
00:49:19,801 --> 00:49:21,380
Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) was hesitating.

681
00:49:21,681 --> 00:49:23,815
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him: Show me where it is?

682
00:49:24,092 --> 00:49:27,498
Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) pointed to the word because Rasool Allah ﷺ is Ummi(أمِّي), illiterate

683
00:49:27,744 --> 00:49:29,592
 and Rasool Allah ﷺ erased it with his finger.

684
00:49:32,651 --> 00:49:38,273
So Suhail Ibn Amr(سهيل إبن عمرو) was a very tough bargainer not easy to negotiate with.

685
00:49:40,147 --> 00:49:42,693
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه continues by saying.

686
00:49:43,619 --> 00:49:47,221
"I have seen, Suhail Ibn Amr(سهيل إبن عمرو) two years later

687
00:49:47,522 --> 00:49:50,715
after Sulhal Hudaybiyyah(صلح الحديبيه) in Hajja-tul-Wida(حجَّة الوداع)

688
00:49:50,899 --> 00:49:53,001
Suhail Ibn Amr(سهيل إبن عمرو) has now became Muslim.

689
00:49:54,333 --> 00:49:57,403
He says, Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) said: I have seen him with my own eyes

690
00:49:58,501 --> 00:50:02,256
bringing the camels to Rasool Allah ﷺ, so Rasool Ullah can slaughter them.

691
00:50:03,487 --> 00:50:06,575
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ shaved his hair after Hajj(حَجْ)

692
00:50:07,010 --> 00:50:10,340
and I've seen with my own eyes, Suhail Ibn Amr(سهيل إبن عمرو)

693
00:50:10,392 --> 00:50:16,606
going down on his knees, picking up the hair clippings of Rasool Allah ﷺ and putting them on his eyes,

694
00:50:17,495 --> 00:50:19,731
 to get the blessings of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

695
00:50:21,477 --> 00:50:23,242
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه said:

696
00:50:23,432 --> 00:50:27,955
These are the results and I thanked Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ for guiding him to Islam.

697
00:50:28,589 --> 00:50:32,724
If we would have hasten things Islam wouldn't have spread the way it did.

698
00:50:33,065 --> 00:50:34,636
Because of Sulhal Hudaybiyyah(صلح الحديبيه).

699
00:50:35,227 --> 00:50:36,258
تحاجز الناس

700
00:50:36,282 --> 00:50:40,613
War was stopped and that was when the Da'wah(دعوة) was spread all over Arabia

701
00:50:40,653 --> 00:50:44,105
because now the Sahabah(صحابه) can go out in Da'wah(دعوة) without fear.

702
00:50:44,772 --> 00:50:48,300
And that is when the people started to come into Islam in multifolds.

703
00:50:49,258 --> 00:50:53,351
When Sulhal Hudaybiyyah(صلح الحديبيه) happened the Muslims were one Thousand 400.

704
00:50:53,961 --> 00:50:57,560
Two years later Rasool Allah ﷺ conquers Makkah with 10,000.

705
00:50:58,806 --> 00:51:10,650
So Rasool Allah ﷺ, in 19 years of Da'wah(دعوة) six plus 13, has 1400

706
00:51:11,045 --> 00:51:15,384
and in just two years because of Sulhal Hudaybiyyah(صلح الحديبيه), he now has 10,000.

707
00:51:16,763 --> 00:51:18,671
These were the results of Sulhal Hudaybiyyah(صلح الحديبيه).

708
00:51:18,941 --> 00:51:22,387
People, they fail to see the wisdom in Sulhal Hudaybiyyah(صلح الحديبيه)

709
00:51:24,852 --> 00:51:25,870
As-Suyuti(السيوطي) says:

710
00:51:26,054 --> 00:51:31,712
لقد كان صديق أسدَّ الصحابه راعيً واَكْمَلَهُم عَقْلَ

711
00:51:32,396 --> 00:51:38,158
As-Suyuti(السيوطي) says that the Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه had the best opinion among the Sahabah(صحابه)

712
00:51:38,337 --> 00:51:40,457
and he had the most complete mind among them.

713
00:51:43,149 --> 00:51:45,991
Again, Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه would lead armies.

714
00:51:46,355 --> 00:51:48,184
Salama Ibn Aqwa(سلمة بن ألاكوع) he says:

715
00:51:48,977 --> 00:51:55,794
بعث رسول الله صلي الله عليه وسلم أبا بكر الى نجد وَ أمَّرهو علينا فبيتنا الناسً من هوازن

716
00:51:56,134 --> 00:52:01,641
فقتلت بيدي سبعت أهل الأبيات وكان شيعارُنَا أمت أمت

717
00:52:02,388 --> 00:52:06,441
Salama Ibn Aqwa(سلمة بن ألاكوع) said: Rasool Allah ﷺ sent us in an army

718
00:52:06,648 --> 00:52:09,452
led by Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه to Najd(نجد)

719
00:52:09,956 --> 00:52:12,467
فبيتنا الناسً من هوازن

720
00:52:12,491 --> 00:52:14,192
At-Tabeet(أتبيت) is attacking at night.

721
00:52:14,657 --> 00:52:19,116
And this form of warfare is where most of the collateral damage occurs

722
00:52:19,228 --> 00:52:24,747
 because it's at night and you're attacking people in their villages

723
00:52:25,105 --> 00:52:28,202
so eventually some children or women get killed.

724
00:52:28,737 --> 00:52:31,524
And this is something that this scholars is talked about in the books of Fiqh(فقه),

725
00:52:31,549 --> 00:52:32,827
the Hukm(حكم) of Tabeet(أتبيت),

726
00:52:33,354 --> 00:52:34,187
تبيت ألعدوَ

727
00:52:34,212 --> 00:52:39,453
Attacking at night because it's in darkness, and it's happened a few times in the time of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

728
00:52:40,001 --> 00:52:41,371
 you have to do what you have to do.

729
00:52:41,492 --> 00:52:47,191
So Sahabah رضي الله عنهم in few situations could not get into a situation where an army is meeting an army

730
00:52:47,231 --> 00:52:48,466
 so that they would attack at night.

731
00:52:48,931 --> 00:52:50,574
So Salama Ibn Aqwa(سلمة بن ألاكوع) says:

732
00:52:50,635 --> 00:52:54,170
I have killed the inhabitants of seven houses, myself.

733
00:52:56,186 --> 00:52:59,452
And he said: Our shu'ar(شعار) was Amit(أمت), Amit(أمت), Kill! Kill! was our slogan

734
00:52:59,784 --> 00:53:01,646
they used to have a slogan in every battle.

735
00:53:02,550 --> 00:53:05,962
Depending on the battle it would be different slogan that was something that was promoted

736
00:53:06,318 --> 00:53:10,310
you have to have certain banners with a certain color your symbol

737
00:53:10,625 --> 00:53:14,535
 and then you have to have a certain slogan that you repeat in the battleground.

738
00:53:14,871 --> 00:53:16,835
It is something that was Rasool Allah ﷺ did

739
00:53:16,949 --> 00:53:20,547
and it was a tradition that was carried on by the Sahabah(صحابه), after him.

740
00:53:20,649 --> 00:53:23,982
So their slogan that day was Amit(أمت), Amit(أمت).

741
00:53:24,774 --> 00:53:29,262
In the Battle of Zatis Salasal(ذات السلاسل), I'll mentioned two things that happened

742
00:53:29,657 --> 00:53:34,064
Zatis Salasal(ذات السلاسل) was an army led by Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص)

743
00:53:34,435 --> 00:53:39,324
and it had Suraat As-Sahabah(صُرات الصحابة), it had the leaders and the elders among the Sahabah(صحابه) among in it.

744
00:53:39,815 --> 00:53:42,873
Now Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) was a newcomer to Islam, he was a late Muslim

745
00:53:43,393 --> 00:53:46,658
he only became Muslim after Sulhal Hudaybiyyah(صلح الحديبيه).

746
00:53:47,443 --> 00:53:53,086
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ appoints him in an army that had the early Muslims.

747
00:53:53,146 --> 00:54:02,963
And in Islam, the early is considered to be higher, As-Sabiqa(ألسابقه) being early in Islam is a virtue.

748
00:54:03,687 --> 00:54:06,579
So here you have Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) who was a late comer in Islam.

749
00:54:06,755 --> 00:54:09,398
Suddenly, he is being appointed to lead an army.

750
00:54:09,762 --> 00:54:13,070
So that was something that the Sahabah(صحابه)

751
00:54:13,163 --> 00:54:15,647
Ya'ani(يعني) it raised the attention of the Sahabah(صحابه) that

752
00:54:16,237 --> 00:54:19,110
Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) is suddenly now leading an army and he just became a Muslim.

753
00:54:19,747 --> 00:54:26,478
Anyway, Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) after he decided where they should camp for the night, he said:

754
00:54:26,989 --> 00:54:32,862
Do not light, any campfires, I don't want any campfires, around.

755
00:54:33,397 --> 00:54:35,171
And the desert could be very cold at night

756
00:54:36,034 --> 00:54:38,547
and you need fire to walk around, to see your direction

757
00:54:38,848 --> 00:54:40,888
 to get warmth to heat your waters.

758
00:54:41,049 --> 00:54:46,229
And Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) is giving his clear orders to the army, Not to have any campfires

759
00:54:46,959 --> 00:54:48,187
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was upset

760
00:54:48,211 --> 00:54:50,429
I mean why he is, why he is telling us not to have any fire

761
00:54:51,105 --> 00:54:52,662
and he went back to Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) and said:

762
00:54:52,686 --> 00:54:54,990
What was going on, how come he doesn't want us to have any fire?

763
00:54:57,713 --> 00:55:00,120
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه told Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب)

764
00:55:00,913 --> 00:55:04,849
He said: Rasool Allah ﷺ would not appoint him to lead an army

765
00:55:06,220 --> 00:55:11,248
and make you a follower in this army, unless this man has some knowledge with warfare.

766
00:55:12,885 --> 00:55:16,661
Rasool Allah ﷺ would not put him in this position and make him lead you

767
00:55:16,986 --> 00:55:18,908
unless he knows what he's doing.

768
00:55:20,842 --> 00:55:25,043
Therefore Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) accepted and he didn't go to Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص).

769
00:55:25,226 --> 00:55:27,085
Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) was saying:

770
00:55:28,159 --> 00:55:33,452
There is Hikmah(حكمة), there's wisdom in Rasool Allah ﷺ choosing Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص), who just became Muslim to lead an Army.

771
00:55:34,378 --> 00:55:37,700
Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص), had the character of a leader.

772
00:55:38,173 --> 00:55:39,810
He had intelligence in warfare

773
00:55:40,599 --> 00:55:42,952
and Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) would later come to realize this

774
00:55:42,976 --> 00:55:44,614
because when Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was a Khalifah(خليفه)

775
00:55:44,969 --> 00:55:47,814
he once saw Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) walking, He said,

776
00:55:48,225 --> 00:55:50,464
This man was born to be a leader.

777
00:55:52,492 --> 00:55:55,505
It is not appropriate for Amr(عمرو), except to be an Ameer(أمير)

778
00:55:55,674 --> 00:55:56,943
by just the way he walks.

779
00:55:58,457 --> 00:56:01,539
And Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) was appointed by Rasool Allah ﷺ

780
00:56:01,563 --> 00:56:06,215
in the life of Rasool Allah ﷺ  and he was his Governor over Oman(عمان).

781
00:56:06,781 --> 00:56:09,418
And when Abu Bakr Siddique رضي الله عنه became Khalifah(خليفه),

782
00:56:09,758 --> 00:56:12,706
he appointed him to go and fight in Falestine(فلسطين).

783
00:56:13,062 --> 00:56:16,695
And then later on he was appointed to be the governor of Egypt

784
00:56:17,019 --> 00:56:19,887
 where he was the governor for a few decades.

785
00:56:20,508 --> 00:56:23,287
He remained the governor of Egypt for a very, very long time.

786
00:56:24,752 --> 00:56:27,901
The second incident worthy of mention:

787
00:56:29,359 --> 00:56:36,233
The army was going to faraway land, Tae(طيئ) they needed some direction.

788
00:56:37,296 --> 00:56:40,815
So Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) was asking for the best guide.

789
00:56:42,069 --> 00:56:44,692
So they brought him Rafea Bin Amr At-Taae(رافع بن عمروألطائ).

790
00:56:45,876 --> 00:56:49,469
Rafea Bin Amr At-Taae(رافع بن عمروألطائ), he was a thief, that what he was.

791
00:56:49,579 --> 00:56:53,896
He was a thief, he was a type of thief, who would raid caravans alone.

792
00:56:54,979 --> 00:56:59,264
You had organized gangs groups that would attack caravans

793
00:56:59,288 --> 00:57:02,900
and then you had these lonely figures who would do their own thing.

794
00:57:03,280 --> 00:57:05,779
They don't need any gangs, they would just attack on their own

795
00:57:06,276 --> 00:57:09,228
they have enough confidence in themselves to do it by themselves.

796
00:57:10,451 --> 00:57:12,427
Rafea bin Amr(رافع بن عمرو) was one of these characters.

797
00:57:12,634 --> 00:57:16,713
He would go on his own he is his own army and he would go and raid caravans.

798
00:57:17,888 --> 00:57:19,437
This was the best they could find.

799
00:57:20,207 --> 00:57:26,335
He was the best guide he knows his way around the path of the desert very well, because that's his job.

800
00:57:28,019 --> 00:57:32,353
So they hired him to take them around so he spent time with this Muslim army

801
00:57:32,646 --> 00:57:35,142
he was quite impressed with what he saw.

802
00:57:36,666 --> 00:57:39,253
So, and he narrates this he says;

803
00:57:39,437 --> 00:57:42,331
So I came to Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق), he didn't know him yet

804
00:57:43,968 --> 00:57:46,669
He said: I saw this man who had this cloth on

805
00:57:47,166 --> 00:57:49,913
whenever he is riding he would hold the cloth of the pin

806
00:57:50,308 --> 00:57:54,278
and then whenever he sits down, he would take out that pin and take off the clothes.

807
00:57:54,712 --> 00:57:55,897
So I went to him and said:

808
00:57:55,921 --> 00:57:56,960
يا صاحب الخلال

809
00:57:57,261 --> 00:57:58,576
O you the one with a pin.

810
00:58:00,080 --> 00:58:02,012
إني توسمتك من بين الصحابك

811
00:58:02,399 --> 00:58:06,080
I can see on you, some marks of intelligence

812
00:58:08,397 --> 00:58:12,108
and I'm choosing you out of all of the people, because I have a question for you?

813
00:58:13,362 --> 00:58:16,283
Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) says: What do you want?

814
00:58:16,365 --> 00:58:21,270
He said: I want you to teach me something, so I can be like you.

815
00:58:23,196 --> 00:58:25,536
But don't make it long, because then I'm gonna forget.

816
00:58:28,196 --> 00:58:33,788
I mean, I think he fits the profile of a thief, not interested in a lot of education.

817
00:58:34,143 --> 00:58:37,596
Give me something brief and fast, I want to be like you, but make it easy.

818
00:58:38,318 --> 00:58:39,493
Tell them how to be like you!

819
00:58:39,517 --> 00:58:40,854
لا تطول علي لا فأنس

820
00:58:40,879 --> 00:58:41,768
Don't make it long,

821
00:58:42,359 --> 00:58:44,946
Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) made it as easy as he could.

822
00:58:45,263 --> 00:58:47,896
He said: Do you remember that your hand has five fingers.

823
00:58:48,314 --> 00:58:51,434
He said: Yes, I do! He said: Then remember this,

824
00:58:52,069 --> 00:58:52,917
the first finger

825
00:58:53,069 --> 00:58:56,434
اشهدو الله اله إلا الله وأشهدوأنَّ محمدًا رسول الله

826
00:58:57,649 --> 00:58:58,659
The second finger,

827
00:58:59,035 --> 00:59:00,496
you pray five times a day.

828
00:59:01,358 --> 00:59:02,393
The third finger,

829
00:59:03,329 --> 00:59:05,361
you pay Zakah(زكوة) if you have money.

830
00:59:06,099 --> 00:59:07,119
The fourth finger,

831
00:59:07,596 --> 00:59:09,403
you fast in the month of Ramadan(رمضان).

832
00:59:09,695 --> 00:59:11,515
The fifth finger, is

833
00:59:11,555 --> 00:59:12,808
 you make a Hajj(حَجْ) to the house of Allah.

834
00:59:12,983 --> 00:59:14,005
 Did you remember that?

835
00:59:14,222 --> 00:59:17,617
He said: Yes! He said: And I'll add something else.

836
00:59:18,332 --> 00:59:24,671
Never assume a position of authority, even over two people, He said:

837
00:59:25,142 --> 00:59:27,503
وهل تكون إمر إلَّا فيكم أهل المدر

838
00:59:28,859 --> 00:59:32,338
We have given up our position of authority to you, the settlers.

839
00:59:33,341 --> 00:59:37,601
In Arabia the Bedouins used to have this respect for the settlers.

840
00:59:37,621 --> 00:59:41,572
The people of the urban towns, and they would give them the authority.

841
00:59:42,212 --> 00:59:46,905
He said: We don't take authority you know that the authority is for you;

842
00:59:47,125 --> 00:59:47,996
The urban people.

843
00:59:48,789 --> 00:59:50,013
Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) said;

844
00:59:50,275 --> 00:59:55,544
A time will come when there will be so many positions of authority

845
00:59:56,035 --> 00:59:59,573
that it will reach you, and it will even reach the people who are below you.

846
01:00:01,858 --> 01:00:05,989
And when you are a leader among people and there's any oppression that goes on

847
01:00:06,259 --> 01:00:08,489
you will be asked about it on the day of judgment.

848
01:00:10,353 --> 01:00:12,417
And what Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) said: Came true

849
01:00:13,296 --> 01:00:15,975
the Muslim Khilafah(خِلَافَه) grew so fast

850
01:00:16,620 --> 01:00:19,264
and it expanded with a swift speed

851
01:00:19,706 --> 01:00:22,294
that there were so many posts that needed to be filled

852
01:00:22,923 --> 01:00:26,526
and it reached the people like him and the people who are lower than him.

